    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d464">

                <pb facs="0638" n="352" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg352"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/2303</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Page</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 3092</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-02-19">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 19, 1916</hi>
                        </date>.<lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received March 6</hi>.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to the Department’s
                    cablegram No. 2774<anchor n="1" xml:id="d464-f1"/> of January 25, and my
                    telegraphic reply No. 3913 of the 18th instant,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d464-f2"
                    />relative to the possible effects of the Trading with the Enemy (Extension of
                    Powers) Act, 1915, on the commerce of the United States, I have the honor to
                    transmit herewith, for the information of the Department, a copy of the note,
                    dated the 16th instant, which has been addressed to the Embassy by the Foreign
                    Trade Department of the Foreign Office in this connection.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Walter Hines Page</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d464-a1.xml" xpointer="d464-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
